- op: discuss  # 6544
  at: '2026-08-16T04:59:42Z'  # 6544
  by: agent  # 6544
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6544
  clock: 3  # 6544
  nonce: '6544'  # 6544
  message: "SATISFIED at dev 4e8c47e47d (PRs #365+#366). Resolved BY ROWS, revising this item's own filed root-cause: the attribute row speaks about REFERENCE edges, the new os.environ.*/sys.stdout.*/sys.stderr.*/sys.stdin.* rows about CALL edges - two edge shapes, two facts, so rows are not a second home and no join change is needed. One correction the gate itself forced: the rows are kind functions:, not methods:, because the analyzer emits these attribute-chain calls with call_construct=None and a methods: kind trips the method-starvation check (measured: 18/18 inconclusive on exactly that, the tokenizers lesson repeated). Behavioral evidence on the merged tree: os.environ.get -> env_read, sys.stdout.write -> logging, sys.stdin.read -> ipc_recv (test_io_primitives_python_climb::TestTheSlotFamily), and the four attribute modules are gone from unknown."  # 6544
